From 711046f91007798f740b869dfa335d20ced0d0a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:00:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: publish what native Dolby Vision output is doing

The player information dialog could only show the profile and, through
VideoPlayer.HdrDetail, whether an HDMI DV frame was presented. To check
Dolby Vision playback from the player, publish its state as properties
of the Home window, read by the skin:

- hades.dv.state: "native" while DV frames reach the display;
- hades.dv.reason: why native output is not used (failed, display,
  output, range, mode), a short form of the SupportsNativeDVOutput()
  verdict that is already logged;
- hades.dv.display: standard, lowlatency or none, from the EDID;
- hades.dv.layers (FEL, MEL or BL) and hades.dv.cm (4.0 or 2.9) of the
  last presented frame, with the same FEL test as CDVPlaybackInfo;
- hades.dv.l1 (min / avg / max in cd/m2, from the 12-bit PQ codes),
  hades.dv.l2 (number of trims), hades.dv.l5 (active area offsets) and
  hades.dv.l6 (MaxCLL / MaxFALL) of that frame;
- hades.dv.mode: the output mode with its exact refresh rate;
- hades.dv.shown, hades.dv.notshown, hades.dv.gap (ms) and
  hades.dv.l1changes: the last complete 10-s statistics window, the
  same numbers that are logged, plus how many presented frames carried
  a different L1 than the previous one.

Values are formatted without words, so that the skin localizes the
labels. They are published from PresentRender() on the main thread,
at most twice a second and only when they change, and once more when
DV output ends; every key is always written, empty when it does not
apply, so nothing stale remains.
